{"text": "BO\n\nPHILIP MORRIS\n\nU.S.A.\n\u201cWOPARK AVENUE. NEW YORK, MY 1007-8882, TELEPHONE 2) 8605000\n\nAugust 16, 1992\n\nMr. Roberto Y. Hernandez\nMission Economic Cultural Association\n3007 24th Street\nSan Francisco, California 94110\n\nth Street Festi: cal\nDear Mr. Hernandez:\n\nThis letter constitutes the agreement between Philip Morris\nIncorporated (\"Philip Morris\") and the Mission Economic Cultural\nAssociation (\"Promoter\"), regarding Philip Morris\u2019 sponsorship,\non behalf of its Marlboro brand of cigarettes, of the 24th street\nFestival de las americas (the \"Event\") to be held September 15,\n1991 in San Francisco, California. The terms of our agreement\nfollow:\n\n1. | Sponsorship Rights. As a sponsor of the Event, Philip\nMorris will be entitled to the following:\n\n(a) exclusive tobacco sponsorship of the Event;\n\n(b) exclusive sponsorship of the Festival stage and\nthe right to approve in advance the artists to appear on the\nFestival stage;\n\n(c) the right to hang banners and signage on and\naround the Festival Stage and at other locations at the site of\nthe Event to be mutually agreed upon by the parties;\n\n(a) the right to distribute Marlboro buy-one-get-one\nfree coupons and incentive items from a 10' x 20 promotional\nbooth to be supplied by the Promoter; and,\n\n(e) the right to recognition in advertising placed in\n\nconnection with the Event and to approve in advance all materials\nand announcements prepared by Promoter that mention Philip Morris\n\nMARLBORO BENSON HEOGES MERIT VIAGNAGLMS PARUAMENTUGHTS PLAYERS SARATOGA CAMBRIDGE ALPINE MUUTFLTER\n\nBT6ee0s90z",
